    "When the aircraft carries a heavy bomb, fuel efficiency is 2 km/liter, and when it carries a light bomb, it is 3 km/liter — does the loaded efficiency depend only on the type of bomb carried (heavy vs. light), regardless of which target is being attacked?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking whether fuel efficiency is determined solely by bomb type, independent of the target."
}

