    "If multiple bombs are dropped on the same part, is the probability that the part survives the product of the individual survival probabilities (i.e., independent per-bomb destruction attempts), so that the destruction probability for n bombs is 1 minus the product of (1 minus p) for each bomb?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the mathematical method for calculating cumulative destruction probability when multiple bombs are used."
}

{
